James Rising discussed a prospective PhD applicant, M. Ariquzzaman Tiash, who inquired about supervision opportunities in various academic programs at the University of Delaware. Key points included identifying confusion regarding program specifics, particularly that Tiash is interested in the PhD in Environmental Economics. He noted his impressive background in engineering and climate policy, tying into alignment with Rising's research. Rising clarified he is not accepting new PhD students for the 2027 cycle but acknowledged Tiash's qualifications and interests. A draft response was formulated, thanking Tiash for his inquiry and wishing him success in finding a suitable doctoral program.
